# Fingerprints of findings gitleaks should ignore.
#
# Use the commit-independent three-part form:
#
#     <file>:<rule-id>:<start-line>
#
# Do NOT use the four-part <commit>:<file>:<rule-id>:<start-line> form that the
# gitleaks GitHub Action prints in its pull request comment. PRs here are
# squash-merged, so the commit the action names never reaches master. A
# four-part entry silences the finding on the pull request, then stops matching
# once the squash commit exists, so the push scan of master reports the same
# finding again and fails that build.
#
# This file previously carried four-part entries from PR #6800. They named
# commits that never reached master, both files they pointed at have since moved
# or gone, and the allowlist in .gitleaks.toml already excludes src/test/.
# Nothing was left to rewrite, so they are gone.
